# Furious Forebear: "Whenever a creature you control dies while this card is in your graveyard, you may pay {1}{W}. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand." Bot2's Bolt kills the Forebear itself on turn 2: it was not in the graveyard when it died, so nothing triggers (CR 603.10a; `? Stack.Count = 1` as the second Bolt is cast). A second Bolt kills Bot1's Memnite: the ability triggers from the graveyard, Bot1 pays {1}{W} (the Plains and the Mox Jet) and the Forebear returns to its hand - not to the battlefield.

